#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.2.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git 2.46.2 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.2.txt:7
msgid ""
"This release is primarily to merge changes to unbreak the 32-bit GitHub "
"actions jobs we use for CI testing, so that we can release real fixes for "
"the 2.46.x track after they pass CI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.2.txt:12
msgid ""
"It also reverts the \"git patch-id\" change that went into 2.46.1, as it "
"seems to have got a regression reported (I haven't verified, but it is "
"better to keep a known breakage than adding an unintended regression)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.2.txt:14
msgid "Other than that, a handful of minor bugfixes are included."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.2.txt:18
msgid ""
"In a few corner cases \"git diff --exit-code\" failed to report "
"\"changes\" (e.g., renamed without any content change), which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.2.txt:21
msgid ""
"Cygwin does have /dev/tty support that is needed by things like single-key "
"input mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.2.txt:23
msgid ""
"The interpret-trailers command failed to recognise the end of the message "
"when the commit log ends in an incomplete line."
msgstr ""
